<Shell title="About" active="About"><section class="wrap section"><small>PACIFIC NORTHWEST</small><h1>About Shawn</h1><div class="case about"><figure><img src="/media/portrait.webp" alt="Shawn Preston"/></figure><div><h2>GIS developer & climate researcher</h2><p>My work connects environmental science with the practical work of making maps and software. I use Python, R, SQL, ArcGIS Pro and Google Earth Engine to explore how hazards and climate vary across places.</p><h3>Experience</h3><p>My background includes GIS Technician III work at Clark County, a physical scientist student traineeship at NOAA, graduate research at Washington State University and a GIS internship at NASA Marshall Space Flight Center.</p><h3>Education</h3><p>Washington State University, Vancouver<br/>M.S. Environmental Science, 2024<br/>B.S. Environmental Science, 2020</p><a href="/research.html">Explore the research →</a></div></div></section></Shell>
